/surname><given-names>EC</given-names></name><name><surname>Goldberg</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Lawson</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Robinson</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Oestrogenic activity of certain synthetic compounds</article-title><source>Nature</source><year>1938</year><volume>141</volume><fpage>247</fpage><lpage>248</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Robson</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Schonberg</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Fahim</surname><given-names>HA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Duration of action of natural and synthetic estrogens</article-title><source>Nature</source><year>1938</year><volume>142</volume><fpage>292</fpage><lpage>293</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Haddow</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Watkinson</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Paterson</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Influence of synthetic oestrogens upon advanced malignant disease</article-title><source>BMJ</source><year>1944</year><volume>2</volume><fpage>393</fpage><lpage>398</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Greenwald</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Barlow</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Nasca</surname><given-names>PC</given-names></name><name><surname>Burnett</surname><given-names>WS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Vaginal cancer after maternal treatment with synthetic estrogens</article-title><source>N Engl J Med</source><year>1971</year><volume>285</vol